<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Robustness to the decision subspace rank <math id="A5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{dec}}</annotation></semantics></math></h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We re-run the sweep at <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{dec}}\in\{1,2,3,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{dec}}\in\{1,2,3,4\}</annotation></semantics></math> on the
three base models, holding all other settings fixed. Cross-effect
magnitudes <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta M|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta M|</annotation></semantics></math> are independent of <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{dec}}</annotation></semantics></math> by construction
(the intervention uses the raw category subspaces); the ablation therefore
tests the residualized overlap geometry and its correlation with
intervention effects. Table <a href="#A5.T3" title='Table 3 ‣ Appendix E Robustness to the decision subspace rank 𝑘_"dec" ‣ A Low-Rank Subspace Analysis of LLM Interventions' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> reports both
quantities. The mean residualized off-diagonal overlap varies by at most
<math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.08" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.08</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.08</annotation></semantics></math> across the sweep for any model, and the cross-model ranking is
preserved. The Pearson correlation between residualized overlap and
<math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta M|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta M|</annotation></semantics></math> peaks at <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{dec}}\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{dec}}\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math> and decays, and in some
cases reverses sign, at <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{dec}}\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{dec}}\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>, consistent with the
explained-variance profile in which the top-1 to top-2 PCs carry essentially
all decision-aligned variance. We therefore use <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{dec}}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{dec}}=2</annotation></semantics></math> throughout: it captures the dominant decision-aligned variance while avoiding both under-removal (at <math id="A5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{dec}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{dec}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>) and over-residualization (at <math id="A5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{dec}}\geq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{dec}}\geq 3</annotation></semantics></math>), and yields strong overlap–effect correlation across models.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A5.T3.3" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A5.T3.3.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A5.T3.3.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A5.T3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Model</span></th>
