<td id="A6.T5.3.4.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A6.T5.3.4.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.025</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.3.4.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><math id="A6.T5.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="198\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">198</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">198\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T5.3.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T5.3.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A6.T5.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Mistral-7B</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.3.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A6.T5.3.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.301</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.3.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A6.T5.3.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.332</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.3.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A6.T5.3.5.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.0005</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.3.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A6.T5.3.5.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">3.11</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.3.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A6.T5.3.5.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">3.20</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.3.5.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><span id="A6.T5.3.5.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.021</span></td>
<td id="A6.T5.3.5.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb" style="padding-left:4.0pt;padding-right:4.0pt;"><math id="A6.T5.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="147\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">147</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">147\times</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Geometry, intervention magnitudes, and random-null floor across three
instruction-tuned models, averaged over the last 12 decoder layers (<math id="A6.T5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-12\leq L\leq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-12\leq L\leq-1</annotation></semantics></math>).
<span id="A6.T5.23" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overlap</span>: mean off-diagonal subspace similarity between learned category
subspaces, raw / residualized by the rank-2 decision subspace / replaced by random orthonormal
rank-2 subspaces (3 seeds <math id="A6.T5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> 5 categories per layer; matched ambient dimension and rank).
<span id="A6.T5.24" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-effect</span>: real <math id="A6.T5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{B}_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐁</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{B}_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> projection at <math id="A6.T5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha{=}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha{=}1</annotation></semantics></math> measured on TEST split;
<em id="A6.T5.25" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">self</em> is the diagonal mean, <em id="A6.T5.26" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">max-collateral</em> is the per-source mean of the largest
off-diagonal entry. <span id="A6.T5.27" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Random null</span>: mean <math id="A6.T5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta M|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta M|</annotation></semantics></math> averaged across all 15 random
samples and target categories. <span id="A6.T5.28" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">gap</span>: ratio of self to null per-target.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Decomposing overlap into shared and private components </h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To determine whether cross-category transfer arises from a shared representational mechanism or from correlated but category-specific structure, we further decompose overlapping category subspaces into <em id="A7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">shared</em> and <em id="A7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">private</em> components and test their effects via targeted projection interventions. Because behavioral effects also depend on how strongly category representations couple to the decision-aligned subspace, we do not expect shared subspace overlap alone to predict effect magnitude or symmetry. Instead, this analysis tests whether observed cross-category transfer, when present, is mediated by genuinely shared representational dimensions.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We focus on residualized category subspaces at layer <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-8</annotation></semantics></math> (8<sup id="A7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_sup">th</sup> layer from output), where geometric overlap is strongest. For a pair of categories <math id="A7.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="A7.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{m},B_{m^{\prime}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{m},B_{m^{\prime}}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{\mathrm{model}}\times r}</annotation></semantics></math> denote their residualized subspace bases (with <math id="A7.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=2</annotation></semantics></math> throughout). We form the alignment matrix <math id="A7.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=B_{m}^{\top}B_{m^{\prime}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=B_{m}^{\top}B_{m^{\prime}}\in\mathbb{R}^{r\times r}</annotation></semantics></math>
and compute its singular value decomposition <math id="A7.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=U\Sigma V^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=U\Sigma V^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each singular value <math id="A7.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to the cosine of a principal angle between the two subspaces. Singular directions with large <math id="A7.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> identify strongly aligned dimensions across category subspaces.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Shared subspace construction.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=B_{m}^{\top}B_{m^{\prime}}=U\Sigma V^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=B_{m}^{\top}B_{m^{\prime}}=U\Sigma V^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}=\cos\theta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}=\cos\theta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are the principal-angle cosines. For retained indices <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, define <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=B_{m}u_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=B_{m}u_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=B_{m^{\prime}}v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=B_{m^{\prime}}v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We form symmetric directions <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}\propto p_{i}+q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∝</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}\propto p_{i}+q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and orthonormalize them to obtain a low-dimensional <em id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">shared-direction</em> subspace <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{shared}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>shared</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{shared}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The number of retained directions <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is set by a singular-value threshold (below).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Private (residual) directions.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define private directions for category <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> by projecting <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> onto the orthogonal complement of <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{shared}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>shared</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{shared}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A7.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{m}^{\perp}=(I-Q_{\mathrm{shared}}Q_{\mathrm{shared}}^{\top})B_{m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>shared</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>Q</mi><mi>shared</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{m}^{\perp}=(I-Q_{\mathrm{shared}}Q_{\mathrm{shared}}^{\top})B_{m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">followed by orthonormalization (dropping near-zero directions). We construct <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{m^{\prime}}^{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⟂</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{m^{\prime}}^{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> analogously.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\mathrm{shared}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>shared</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\mathrm{shared}}</annotation></semantics></math> need not lie within <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{col}(B_{m})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>col</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{col}(B_{m})</annotation></semantics></math>, this residualization does not, in general, reduce rank by <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. It should be viewed as removing shared-direction components rather than a canonical subspace decomposition.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Choosing <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We retain indices with <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}\geq 0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}\geq 0.5</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{i}\leq 60^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mn>60</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{i}\leq 60^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Validation.</h5>

<div id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We assess the functional role of these subspaces using projection-based interventions on held-out test prompts. We orthonormalize the columns of <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{m^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{m^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> prior to computing <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. Specifically, we independently project out (i) the shared-direction subspace, (ii) the residual (private) subspace of category <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>, and (iii) the residual subspace of category <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, and measure the resulting change in the refusal decision margin <math id="A7.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta M</annotation></semantics></math>. This allows us to examine whether cross-category effects are more strongly associated with shared directions or category-specific components.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span><span id="A7.T6.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shared vs. private intervention effects across models and category pairs (layer <math id="A7.T6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-8</annotation></semantics></math>).</span>
Each category is represented by a rank-2 residualized subspace. The shared dimensionality <math id="A7.T6.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is determined from the singular values of <math id="A7.T6.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{m}^{\top}B_{m^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>B</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{m}^{\top}B_{m^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> (see text). <span id="A7.T6.18" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shared</span> reports the change in refusal margin <math id="A7.T6.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta M</annotation></semantics></math> when projecting out the shared subspace (category <math id="A7.T6.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> / <math id="A7.T6.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>). <span id="A7.T6.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Private (A/B)</span> reports effects from projecting individual private directions of category <math id="A7.T6.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> (left) or <math id="A7.T6.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>m</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> (right). </figcaption>
