<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span><span id="A9.T10.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-effect matrix (Gemma-2-9B-IT, layer -8, <math id="A9.T10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>) for Jailbreak Dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arditi et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.</span> Values are <math id="A9.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> refusal margin (log-probability units) when projecting out each source category’s subspace. Positive values indicate increased refusal, negative values indicate decreased refusal.</figcaption>
