<section id="A12.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">L.2 </span>Intervention strength Ablation</h3>

<div id="A12.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To test whether cross-category effects are driven by overly strong interventions,
we vary the projection strength <math id="A12.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in[0.1,1.0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in[0.1,1.0]</annotation></semantics></math> and measure both the effect
on the target category (self-effect) and the largest effect on any other category
(max collateral effect).
We evaluate this for the <span id="A12.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Deceptive/Malicious</span> <math id="A12.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A12.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">NSFW</span>
intervention at layer <math id="A12.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-8</annotation></semantics></math> (8<sup id="A12.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_sup">th</sup> layer from output), where residualized overlap is high.</p>
</div>
<div id="A12.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A12.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Tables <a href="#A12.T24" title="Table 24 ‣ L.2 Intervention strength Ablation ‣ Appendix L Further Results on Refusal (Synthetic Dataset) ‣ A Low-Rank Subspace Analysis of LLM Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a> and <a href="#A12.T25" title="Table 25 ‣ L.2 Intervention strength Ablation ‣ Appendix L Further Results on Refusal (Synthetic Dataset) ‣ A Low-Rank Subspace Analysis of LLM Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>,
reducing <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> decreases the absolute magnitude of both self and collateral effects.
However, collateral effects remain comparable in scale to the self effect across all
values of <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.
In particular, weakening the intervention reduces its overall impact and does not
eliminate cross-category effects. Private-subspace projections (Appendix <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Decomposing overlap into shared and private components ‣ A Low-Rank Subspace Analysis of LLM Interventions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>) reduce the absolute size of collateral effects relative
to full-subspace projections, but collateral effects persist even at small <math id="A12.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A12.T24" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 24: </span>
<span id="A12.T24.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Self-effects and collateral effects under varying intervention strength (<math id="A12.T24.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>) (Gemma-2-9B-IT).</span>
Self-effect is <math id="A12.T24.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta M(\text{target})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>target</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta M(\text{target})|</annotation></semantics></math> and max collateral is <math id="A12.T24.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max|\Delta M(\text{others})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>others</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max|\Delta M(\text{others})|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Results for <span id="A12.T24.16" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Deceptive/Malicious</span> <math id="A12.T24.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A12.T24.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">NSFW</span> at layer <math id="A12.T24.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-8</annotation></semantics></math> .
</figcaption>
