<figure id="A12.T31" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 31: </span><span id="A12.T31.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Layer-wise mean intervention effects across models.</span>
Self effects are mean absolute <math id="A12.T31.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta M|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta M|</annotation></semantics></math> for diagonal entries (projecting out each category’s own subspace).
Collateral effects are mean absolute <math id="A12.T31.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta M|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta M|</annotation></semantics></math> for off-diagonal entries (cross-category transfer).
Effects are strongest in mid-to-late layers (<math id="A12.T31.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-8</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A12.T31.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-4</annotation></semantics></math>), indicating where overlapping category representations are prominent.
</figcaption>
